From 09f5914abcdc1013e3eba6d4108a15be4675033b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: codEx Fork Bot <codex-fork-bot@localhost>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 21:35:52 +0800
Subject: rewind: restore files only after a successful fork and verify the
 snapshot

- ForkSessionForPromptEdit now carries an optional RewindRestoreRequest
  that is executed only after the fork and thread attach succeed, so a
  failed conversation rewind (steer, in-progress turn, thread switch)
  never rolls back workspace files on its own.
- rewind_restore_files verifies the snapshot's recorded prompt against
  the selected message and resolves drift by picking the closest matching
  snapshot, instead of silently restoring whichever snapshot matches the
  index or falling back to the newest one.
- Removes the standalone RewindRestoreFiles event; the end-to-end test
  now exercises the picker's real mapping (nth + 1) and asserts the files
  are restored to the snapshot taken right before the selected message.
